# Where the local PostgreSQL cluster lives. The single source of these four facts:
# psql, createdb and initdb read them as the PG* variables poe exports from this file,
# and config.py reads the same file to compose the DSN SQLAlchemy connects with. Nothing
# in pixi.toml or pyproject.toml declares them a second time.
#
# 5433 rather than 5432 so the cluster cannot collide with a system PostgreSQL, and the
# loopback address so it is off the network entirely. Both are baked into .pgdata/ by
# `pixi run backend-db-create`, so changing the port here means
# `pixi run backend-db-reset && pixi run backend-db-init` to rebuild the cluster on it.
#
# Committed, and holding development defaults only - the deployed API is handed a
# DATABASE_URL by whoever operates its database. To move the local cluster off a port
# something else has taken, put PGPORT in backend/.env.local, which is gitignored and
# layered over this file by both readers.
PGHOST=127.0.0.1
PGPORT=5433
PGUSER=expense_tracker
PGDATABASE=expense_tracker
